\title{Pipelines}
\meta{toc}{false}

\p{Compose transforms with \code{|}, then pass the pipeline to \code{init}. Stages run left to right and may change several configuration fields. Call \code{pipe()} to inspect the resulting \code{OptimizerConfig}.}

\<section>[id]{baux.enn}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.enn}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.transforms}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.enn}](api-pipelines.html#baux.enn)}}
  \pre{
baux.enn(
    *,
    k: int | None = 10,
    num_samples: int | None = 100,
    scale_x: bool = False,
    index: Any = NeighborIndex.FLAT,
    storage: str | None = None,
    metric_learning: str = 'none',
    geometry: str = 'euclidean',
    local_k: int = 4,
    stiefel: Any = None,
    affine: Any = None,
    tied_dims: tuple[tuple[int, ...], ...] | None = None,
) -> Transform
  }
  \p{Configure an ENN surrogate.}
  \p{Returns a \code{Transform}. \code{k}: neighbor count. \code{num_samples}: leave-one-out fitting sample budget; \code{None} disables that fitting setting. \code{scale_x}: input scaling.}
  \p{\code{index}: a \code{NeighborIndex} or accepted driver name such as \code{"flat"}, \code{"usearch"}, \code{"metal"} or \code{"cuda"}. Hardware support depends on the build. \code{storage}: optional storage selection.}
  \p{\code{metric_learning}, \code{geometry}, \code{local_k}, \code{tied_dims}: input metric and grouping settings. \code{stiefel} and \code{affine}: optional output maps.}
  \p{When the incoming acquisition is random, this transform selects UCB, or Pareto selection if \code{num_samples=None}. An already selected non-random acquisition is preserved.}
  \<div>[class]{api-example}{\<p>[class]{example-label}{Example}
\pre{
import numpy as np
import baux

domain = np.array([[-2.0, 2.0], [-2.0, 2.0]])
pipe = baux.enn(k=8) | baux.ucb(beta=1.5) | baux.lhd(num_init=6) | baux.regions(2)
state = baux.init(domain, pipe, seed=42)
state, y = baux.step(state, lambda x: -np.sum(x**2, axis=-1), num_arms=2)
assert state.num_observations == 2
assert len(y) == 2
print(f"Pipeline obs={state.num_observations} best_y={state.best_y:.5f}")
}
  }
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/transforms.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/transforms.py)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.gp}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.gp}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.transforms}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.gp}](api-pipelines.html#baux.gp)}}
  \pre{
baux.gp() -> Transform
  }
  \p{Configure the Gaussian-process surrogate.}
  \p{Returns a \code{Transform}. If the incoming acquisition is random, selects Thompson sampling. An existing non-random acquisition is preserved.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/transforms.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/transforms.py#L231)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.zero}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.zero}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.transforms}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.zero}](api-pipelines.html#baux.zero)}}
  \pre{
baux.zero() -> Transform
  }
  \p{Configure search without a surrogate.}
  \p{Returns a \code{Transform} that selects \code{NoSurrogate}, random acquisition and a TuRBO region if regions were disabled. Existing active trust-region settings are preserved.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/transforms.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/transforms.py#L247)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.ucb}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.ucb}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.transforms}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.ucb}](api-pipelines.html#baux.ucb)}}
  \pre{
baux.ucb(beta: float = 2.0) -> Transform
  }
  \p{Select candidates by mean plus uncertainty.}
  \p{Returns a \code{Transform} using \code{mu + beta * se}. \code{beta} must be finite and positive. Adds an ENN surrogate if none is configured, and enables ENN fitting when it was disabled.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/transforms.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/transforms.py#L273)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.thompson}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.thompson}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.transforms}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.thompson}](api-pipelines.html#baux.thompson)}}
  \pre{
baux.thompson() -> Transform
  }
  \p{Select candidates using posterior function draws.}
  \p{Returns a \code{Transform}. Adds an ENN surrogate if none is configured, and enables ENN fitting when it was disabled. Use [\code{enn_sample}](api-enn.html#baux.enn_sample) to query function draws directly.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/transforms.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/transforms.py#L287)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.pareto}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.pareto}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.transforms}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.pareto}](api-pipelines.html#baux.pareto)}}
  \pre{
baux.pareto() -> Transform
  }
  \p{Select from the mean–uncertainty frontier.}
  \p{Returns a \code{Transform} using non-dominated sorting over predicted mean and uncertainty. Adds an ENN surrogate if none is configured. This is an acquisition rule; it does not by itself configure multi-objective optimization.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/transforms.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/transforms.py#L301)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.random_acq}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.random_acq}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.transforms}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.random_acq}](api-pipelines.html#baux.random_acq)}}
  \pre{
baux.random_acq() -> Transform
  }
  \p{Select candidates without surrogate scores.}
  \p{Returns a \code{Transform} choosing random acquisition. It leaves the candidate sampler and surrogate configuration in place; use [\code{zero}](api-pipelines.html#baux.zero) to remove the surrogate.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/transforms.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/transforms.py#L318)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.lhd}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.lhd}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.transforms}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.lhd}](api-pipelines.html#baux.lhd)}}
  \pre{
baux.lhd(num_init: int = 10, *, only: bool = False) -> Transform
  }
  \p{Set Latin-hypercube initialization.}
  \p{\code{num_init}: initial evaluation budget. Returns a \code{Transform}. With \code{only=True}, also disables the surrogate and trust region for LHD-only exploration.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/transforms.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/transforms.py#L70)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.sobol}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.sobol}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.transforms}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.sobol}](api-pipelines.html#baux.sobol)}}
  \pre{
baux.sobol(
    num_candidates: int | None = None,
    *,
    per_arm: int | None = None,
    num_pert: int | None = None,
) -> Transform
  }
  \p{Use a scrambled Sobol candidate sampler.}
  \p{Returns a \code{Transform}. \code{num_candidates}: total candidate budget; \code{per_arm}: budget per requested arm. Omitted values preserve the current configuration. \code{num_pert} sets the perturbation count when supplied.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/transforms.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/transforms.py#L115)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.raasp}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.raasp}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.transforms}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.raasp}](api-pipelines.html#baux.raasp)}}
  \pre{
baux.raasp(
    num_pert: int | None = 20,
    *,
    num_candidates: int | None = None,
    per_arm: int | None = None,
    driver: RAASPDriver = RAASPDriver.ORIG,
) -> Transform
  }
  \p{Use sparse coordinate perturbations for candidates.}
  \p{Returns a \code{Transform}. \code{num_pert}: expected perturbation count, capped by dimension; \code{num_candidates} and \code{per_arm} set candidate budgets. Omitted budgets preserve the current configuration.}
  \p{\code{driver} uses \code{RAASPDriver} from \code{baux.turbo.config.candidates}. The default is \code{RAASPDriver.ORIG}.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/transforms.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/transforms.py#L89)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.uniform_pert}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.uniform_pert}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.transforms}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.uniform_pert}](api-pipelines.html#baux.uniform_pert)}}
  \pre{
baux.uniform_pert(
    num_candidates: int | None = None,
    *,
    per_arm: int | None = None,
    num_pert: int | None = None,
) -> Transform
  }
  \p{Use uniform random candidate perturbations.}
  \p{Returns a \code{Transform}. \code{num_candidates}, \code{per_arm} and \code{num_pert} override the respective candidate settings when supplied. This configures candidate generation; acquisition chooses which candidates to evaluate.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/transforms.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/transforms.py#L140)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.regions}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.regions}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.transforms}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.regions}](api-pipelines.html#baux.regions)}}
  \pre{
baux.regions(
    count: int = 4,
    *,
    sharing: Any = 'ellipsoid_ball',
    allocation: Any = 'incumbent_ucb1',
    success_tolerance: int = 3,
    failure_tolerance: int = 5,
    length: TrustRegionBounds | None = None,
) -> Transform
  }
  \p{Enable multiple local search regions.}
  \p{Returns a \code{Transform}. \code{count} is the positive number of regions. Sharing choices are \code{"box_contain"}, \code{"ellipsoid_ball"}, \code{"nearest_center"} and \code{"origin_only"}. The transform defaults to \code{"ellipsoid_ball"}.}
  \p{Allocation choices are \code{"incumbent_ucb1"}, \code{"least_trials"} and \code{"joint_acquisition"}. Positive success and failure tolerances control region resizing; \code{length} supplies explicit bounds.}
  \p{For restart policy, fixed-radius control or per-region acquisitions, use [\code{RegionalSearchPolicy}](api-configuration.html#baux.RegionalSearchPolicy). See [multiple regions and workers](baux-0009.html) for a complete loop.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/transforms.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/transforms.py#L356)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.tr_bounds}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.tr_bounds}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.transforms}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.tr_bounds}](api-pipelines.html#baux.tr_bounds)}}
  \pre{
baux.tr_bounds(
    *,
    length_init: float = 0.8,
    length_min: float = 0.0078125,
    length_max: float = 1.6,
) -> Transform
  }
  \p{Set trust-region length limits.}
  \p{Returns a \code{Transform}. Requires \code{0 < length_min <= length_init <= length_max}. Lengths are in normalized coordinates.}
  \p{Updates length bounds on a regional policy. For other policies, installs a \code{TurboTrustRegion} with these bounds.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/transforms.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/transforms.py#L331)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.with_geometry}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.with_geometry}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.transforms}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.with_geometry}](api-pipelines.html#baux.with_geometry)}}
  \pre{
baux.with_geometry(model: Any, geometry: str, local_k: int = 4) -> Any
  }
  \p{Change the ENN dissimilarity geometry.}
  \p{\code{geometry}: \code{"euclidean"}, \code{"conformal"}, \code{"hyperbolic"} or \code{"wasserstein"}. \code{local_k} must be positive. See [ENN predictions](baux-0003.html) for the formulas behind these names.}
  \p{With an \code{ENNState} or \code{ENN}, returns a model retaining the observations. With a configuration or \code{Transform}, returns its updated configuration.}
  \p{With an \code{OptimizerState}, this function initializes a new optimizer and does not retain the optimization history. Configure geometry before starting a search.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/enn/enn_state.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/enn/enn_state.py#L77)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.stein}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.stein}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.transforms}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.stein}](api-pipelines.html#baux.stein)}}
  \pre{
baux.stein(target: Any = None, frame: Any = None, *, rank: int | None = None) -> Any
  }
  \p{Configure prediction shrinkage toward a subspace.}
  \p{Use \code{stein(rank=F)} to build a pipeline transform, or \code{stein(enn_state, frame)} to apply a supplied \code{Stiefel} frame. A rank requests a frame estimated from observed outputs.}
  \p{The basis has shape \code{(M, F)}. Use \code{Stiefel.from_factors} to orthonormalize supplied factors. This API does not provide a James–Stein risk guarantee.}
  \p{Applying the transform to an \code{OptimizerState} initializes a new optimizer; configure it before collecting observations.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/enn/enn_state.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/enn/enn_state.py#L270)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.calibrate}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.calibrate}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.transforms}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.calibrate}](api-pipelines.html#baux.calibrate)}}
  \pre{
baux.calibrate(target: Any = None, affine: Any = None, *, alpha: float | None = None) -> Any
  }
  \p{Configure an affine correction to predictions.}
  \p{Use \code{calibrate(affine=map)} for a supplied \code{Affine}, or \code{calibrate(alpha=0.1)} to request a fitted correction and residual-quantile scale. Applying it to an \code{ENNState} returns a new state.}
  \p{\code{alpha} is a miscoverage setting in \code{(0, 1)}. Adaptive optimization observations do not automatically satisfy exchangeability or a coverage guarantee.}
  \p{Applying it to an \code{OptimizerState} initializes a new optimizer; configure it before collecting observations.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/enn/enn_state.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/enn/enn_state.py#L299)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.Transform}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.Transform}[data-kind]{class}[data-module]{baux.transforms}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.Transform}](api-pipelines.html#baux.Transform)}}
  \pre{
baux.Transform(name: str, fn: Callable[[OptimizerConfig], OptimizerConfig])
  }
  \p{A composable optimizer configuration update.}
  \p{\code{Transform(name, fn)} wraps \code{fn(config) -> OptimizerConfig}. Combine stages with \code{a | b}; the left stage runs first. Call \code{pipe()} to apply it to the default configuration, or \code{pipe(config)} to modify an existing one.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/transforms.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/transforms.py#L35)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.chain}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.chain}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.transforms}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.chain}](api-pipelines.html#baux.chain)}}
  \pre{
baux.chain(
    *steps: Transform | Callable[[OptimizerConfig], OptimizerConfig] | OptimizerConfig,
) -> OptimizerConfig
  }
  \p{Apply configuration stages from left to right.}
  \p{Returns an \code{OptimizerConfig}. A configuration passed among the stages replaces the accumulated configuration; subsequent transforms modify it. Pass the result to \code{init} or \code{create_optimizer}.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/transforms.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/transforms.py#L57)}
}
